# AmneziaWG server env defaults. Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in.
# The one REQUIRED var has no default on purpose: the entrypoint exits with a
# FATAL line and the container restart-loops until it is set.
#
# Bring-your-own keys: peers are `name:PUBLIC_KEY` pairs, comma-separated.
# Generate each client's keypair on the client (awg genkey | awg pubkey) and
# pass only the PUBLIC key here — private keys never touch the server.
AWG_PEERS=phone:XxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxX0=
# Address pool. The server takes the first address (network+1); peer i
# (0-based, AWG_PEERS order) gets network+2+i. Must NOT overlap the container's
# own subnet (the entrypoint refuses to boot if it does) and must not collide
# with your LAN. Third pool: ipsec uses 10.10.10.0/24, wg uses 10.10.20.0/24.
AWG_POOL=10.10.30.0/24
# HeaderProtectionKey — a shared secret, `awg genkey` output, must be THE SAME
# on the server (this var) and in every client conf. Empty = header protection
# off (still valid: the S/H paddings alone already obfuscate).
AWG_HPK=
# Where decrypted client traffic goes: the vpndogs router's SOCKS in. Change
# these only if the router does not listen at its default address/port.
CHAIN_SOCKS_HOST=vpndogs-router
CHAIN_SOCKS_PORT=1070
